===Parliamentary republics with an executive presidency===
{{main|Parliamentary republics with an executive presidency}}
A combined head of state and head of government in the form of an [[executive president]]. In effect, "presidents" in this system function the same as prime ministers do in other [[parliamentary system]]s.

====Parliamentary republics with indirectly elected executive presidency====
Presidency is elected by the legislature and they must maintain the confidence of the legislature to remain in office.

{{colbegin|colwidth=40em}}
*{{flag|Botswana}}{{efn|content=The president is elected by the parliament and holds a parliamentary seat (as an ''[[ex officio member]]''), much like a prime minister. If a vote of no confidence is successful and they do not resign, it triggers the dissolution of the legislature and new elections (per section 92 of the [[Constitution of Botswana|Constitution]]).}}
