====Directorial republic====
{{main|Politics of Switzerland|Directorial system}}
{{flag|Switzerland}} employs a [[Federal Council (Switzerland)|Federal Council]] which jointly exercises the powers of the head of state and government collectively. The Federal Council is elected by the [[Federal Assembly (Switzerland)|Assembly]] but is not subject to [[parliamentary confidence]] during its fixed term. The [[President of the Swiss Confederation|President]] is the Presiding member of the Federal Council in a ''[[primus inter pares]]'' (first among equals) capacity and has no powers over other members of the directory.

